# Build context for every image is the repository root; all Dockerfile paths are
# repo-relative. Everything is excluded by default, re-included explicitly.
#
# The leading `*` is what keeps artifacts/ out. The context is hashed and
# transferred on every build; the 950PR archive alone is 3.1 GB.
# See docs/repository-layout.md.
*

# Offline payload. Bind-mounted at build time, never COPYed.
!deps

# Not read by any Dockerfile. The vLLM checkout exists only so provisioning can
# build its wheel; .provision is scratch; src tarballs are delivery vehicles for
# trees extracted beside them.
deps/src/vllm
deps/.provision
deps/950pr-x86_64/src/vllm
deps/950pr-x86_64/src/*.tar.gz

# Target scaffolds: Dockerfile, entrypoint, verify suite, package lists,
# constraints, manifests and patches.
!targets

# Shared scripts, base stage and vendor shims. Bind-mounted into build RUN
# steps and into provisioning containers, so it must stay in the context.
!common

# Cross-compilation toolchain image.
!builders

# Final deployable archives. Redundant while `*` stands; explicit so a later
# broad re-include cannot expose them.
artifacts
artifacts/**
*.tar.gz

# ...except the googletest source, which IS part of the offline payload.
# `*.tar.gz` above is unanchored, so it matches at any depth and would drop
# deps/builder-x86_64/googletest-*.tar.gz from the context. The Dockerfile only
# WARNS when it cannot find it, so the loss shows up much later as csrc/tests
# trying to clone googletest from github.com inside a --network=none build.
# Last matching pattern wins, so this has to come after.
!deps/builder-x86_64/googletest-*.tar.gz
